      "title": "Branches and PRs: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Branches and PRs: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Branch and PR Defined",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==branch== is a movable **pointer** to a commit",
                "Creating one copies ==no files==: cheap, short-lived by design",
                "A ==pull request== asks GitHub to merge a {blue:head} branch into a {green:base} branch",
                "The PR carries discussion, review and CI checks"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch -c feat/login-form"
              ],
              "note": "new pointer at the current commit"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Feature-Branch Flow",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "main",
                    "sub": "deployable",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Branch off",
                    "sub": "feat/...",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Commits",
                    "sub": "all work here",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "PR",
                    "sub": "review + CI",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "main",
                    "sub": "merged",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==main stays deployable==: never commit straight to it",
                "The PR is the ==gate== back into main"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Naming and Size",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`feat/short-topic`",
                  "`feat/login-form`"
                ],
                [
                  "`fix/short-topic`",
                  "`fix/null-cart`"
                ],
                [
                  "`chore/short-topic`",
                  "`chore/bump-deps`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Format: `type/short-topic`, ==lowercase kebab case==",
                "Keep branches short-lived and small"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Size rule",
              "text": "Under ==~400 changed lines== gets real review. A huge PR gets a **rubber stamp**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core Workflow: Branch to Merge",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Core Workflow: Branch to Merge",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Loop",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Update main",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Branch off",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Commit",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Push",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Open PR",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Review",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fix",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Merge",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Delete branch",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Start and Publish",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch main && git pull --ff-only && git switch -c feat/login-form",
                "git push -u origin feat/login-form",
                "git push"
              ],
              "note": "-u sets upstream once; later plain git push works"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Open the PR from the pushed branch: link in push output, or `gh pr create --fill`",
                "Mark ==Draft== while work is not ready for review"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Review and Clean Up",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fix feedback with ==new commits== on the same branch",
                "Pushing updates the PR **automatically**",
                "Remote branch: GitHub button or auto-delete setting"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch main && git pull && git branch -d feat/login-form"
              ],
              "note": "after merge"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never commit straight to main: every change goes through a branch and a PR."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Keeping a Branch Up to Date",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Keeping a Branch Up to Date",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Fetch First",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git fetch origin` shows what changed upstream",
                "==Never touches== your branch or files",
                "Then pick: merge or rebase `origin/main`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Merge or Rebase",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Merge",
                "Rebase"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Command",
                  "`git merge origin/main`",
                  "`git rebase origin/main`"
                ],
                [
                  "History",
                  "merge commit, as it happened",
                  "linear, commits replayed"
                ],
                [
                  "Hashes",
                  "same",
                  "==rewritten=="
                ],
                [
                  "Shared branch",
                  "{green:safe}",
                  "{red:risky}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Rebase rule",
              "items": [
                "Rebase only commits ==nobody else has pulled==",
                "After rebasing a pushed branch: `git push --force-with-lease`",
                "Never plain `--force`"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Conflicts & GitHub",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Edit files",
                    "sub": "fix markers",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "git add",
                    "sub": "mark resolved",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "--continue",
                    "sub": "merge or rebase",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "--abort",
                    "sub": "bail out",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "GitHub ==Update branch== merges base into your branch",
                "Quick catch-up: use the button",
                "Team wants linear history: rebase locally"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Merge or rebase?** Merge keeps history, safe when shared; rebase is linear but rewrites hashes",
                "**Why --force-with-lease?** It refuses to overwrite commits you have not seen",
                "**Conflict mid-rebase?** Fix, `git add`, `git rebase --continue`, or `--abort`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Opening and Reviewing a Pull Request",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Opening and Reviewing a Pull Request",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Opening a Good PR",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Title: ==what changed==, short and specific",
                "Description: what, why, how tested",
                "`Closes #123` {green:auto-closes} the issue on merge",
                "==Self-review== the diff on GitHub before requesting reviewers",
                "Remove ==debug code== and unrelated changes"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "markdown",
              "lines": [
                "## What",
                "## Why",
                "## How tested",
                "Closes #123"
              ],
              "note": "description skeleton"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reviewing",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Outcome",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Comment",
                  "No verdict"
                ],
                [
                  "Approve",
                  "Good to merge"
                ],
                [
                  "Request changes",
                  "**Blocks merge** if protection requires reviews"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Review the ==code==, not the person",
                "Ask questions instead of commanding",
                "Prefix minor items with `nit:`",
                "Explain ==why== for every blocker"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Author Manners and Speed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Respond to ==every comment==",
                "Resolve a thread only after fixing or agreeing",
                "No ==force-push== mid-review without saying so",
                "Review within ==one working day==",
                "{green:Small PRs} get reviewed faster"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Resolve only after a fix or agreement; announce any force-push."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "GitHub Merge Options and Branch Protection",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "GitHub Merge Options and Branch Protection",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Merge Options",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Option",
                "Lands on main",
                "Log"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Merge commit**",
                  "all branch commits + a merge commit",
                  "full history, ==noisiest=="
                ],
                [
                  "**Squash and merge**",
                  "one commit per PR",
                  "clean, but per-commit detail lost; branch commits no longer match main"
                ],
                [
                  "**Rebase and merge**",
                  "each commit replayed, new hashes",
                  "==linear==, no merge commit"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Branch Protection on main",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Require a pull request== before merging",
                "Set the ==required approvals== count",
                "Require ==status checks== to pass",
                "Require branches ==up to date== with main",
                "==Block force pushes== and deletions"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==CODEOWNERS== review: owned paths need the owning team's approval",
                "Enable ==dismiss stale approvals== on new pushes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "text",
              "lines": [
                "/payments/  @acme/payments-team",
                "/docs/      @acme/docs-team"
              ],
              "note": ".github/CODEOWNERS: path, then owning team"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Admins bypass} protection: apply the rules to admins too",
                "Reusing a ==squash-merged== branch brings old commits back as duplicates"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "After a squash merge",
              "text": "==Delete the branch==. Start the next PR from a fresh branch off main, or it hits duplicate-commit conflicts."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Branches and PRs Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Branches and PRs Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Branch, Sync, Publish",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==fetch== first, then `merge` or `rebase` onto origin/main",
                "After a rebase push with ==--force-with-lease=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch -c feat/login-form",
                "git branch -vv  # list + upstream",
                "git branch -d feat/login-form  # merged",
                "git fetch origin",
                "git rebase origin/main  # or: git merge",
                "git push --force-with-lease  # if rebased"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git push -u origin feat/login-form",
                "gh pr create --fill",
                "gh pr checkout 123  # review locally"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Merge Choice",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Option",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Merge commit",
                  "**full history**"
                ],
                [
                  "Squash",
                  "**one clean commit** per PR"
                ],
                [
                  "Rebase",
                  "**linear**, all commits"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Protection on main",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Require a ==pull request==",
                "Required ==approvals==",
                "Required ==status checks==",
                "Branch ==up to date==",
                "==No force push==",
                "==CODEOWNERS== review"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Top Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Huge PRs",
                "Rebasing shared branches",
                "Plain `--force`",
                "Committing straight to main",
                "Reusing a squash-merged branch"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You rebased a pushed branch onto main and plain `git push` is rejected. What do you run, and why not `--force`?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`git push --force-with-lease`",
                "The rebase rewrote hashes, so your branch diverged from the remote",
                "The lease fails if a teammate pushed meanwhile; `--force` would overwrite their work"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You squash-merged feat/a, kept committing on it, then opened a second PR. What goes wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Squash put one new commit on main; the branch's original commits are not in main's history",
                "The second PR replays them, causing duplicate-commit conflicts",
                "Branch off fresh main for each PR"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A PR had one approval. You push a fix and the merge is blocked again. Which setting caused it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Dismiss stale approvals on new pushes",
                "The old approval is cleared, so a fresh review is needed"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A reviewer chose Comment, not Request changes, but left a serious concern. Is the merge blocked?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No: Comment gives no verdict",
                "Only Request changes blocks, and only when protection requires reviews",
                "Blocking concerns need Request changes, with a reason"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}